%S A400881 1,1,2,6,21,84,365,1696,8287,42146,221383,1194310,6588823,37048242,
%T A400881 211762404,1227800670,7208589543,42794919790,256585250332,
%U A400881 1552128503360,9464640534050,58135013155354,359458448025994,2236108374178094,13988018295583591
%N A400881 Number of s-meandric permutations of length n.
%C A400881 A permutation is said to be s-meandric if it is realizable by a singular open meander. Each permutation is counted once, regardless of its number of realizations.
%H A400881 Yury Belousov, <a href="https://github.com/YuryBelousov/s_meandric">C++ code for generating the sequence</a>, GitHub.
%H A400881 Yury Belousov and Viktoriia Georgievskaia, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.30068">S-meandric Permutations and Tangency Polynomials</a>, arXiv:2609.30068 [math.CO], 2026.
%F A400881 a(0) = 1; a(n) = Sum_{k=1..n} a(n-k)*A400882(k) for n >= 1.
%e A400881 All six permutations of length 3 are s-meandric.
%e A400881 For length 4, exactly 2413, 3142, and 3412 are excluded; a(4)=21.
%Y A400881 Cf. A400882, A393122.
%K A400881 nonn
%O A400881 0,3
